guide.approach:
**Dry run:** the context is cancelled after 30 ms and `d` is one second. The `select` is blocked on both channels; at 30 ms `ctx.Done()` becomes ready; the function returns `context.Canceled` at once.

```go
func WaitOrCancel(ctx context.Context, d time.Duration) error {
	timer := time.NewTimer(d)
	defer timer.Stop()
	select {
	case <-timer.C:
		return nil
	case <-ctx.Done():
		return ctx.Err()
	}
}
```

The explicit timer with `Stop` releases the timer as soon as the function returns early.

